Article 31 (Performance Verification of Fire Equipment) (1) Where the head of a fire service agency intends to extend the period of use of fire equipment whose service life has expired pursuant to Article 27 (3) of the Act, he or she shall conduct a performance assessment of the relevant fire equipment or verify whether it meets the criteria for extension of the period of use determined by the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency: Provided, That performance assessment shall be conducted for the following fire equipment: <Amended on Dec. 15, 2020>
  1. Fire pumper;
  2. Fire water tanker;
  3. Chemical fire truck;
  4. Aerial fire truck;
  5. Salvage tender (only applicable where such vehicles are installed with special devices such as a crane, or towing device);
  6. Other fire equipment determined by the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency.
  (2) Where the head of a fire service agency conducts performance assessment pursuant to paragraph (1), he or she may, if necessary, organize and operate a performance assessment team comprising relevant experts or request the Fire Institute or the fire equipment maintenance center under Article 39 to conduct the whole or part of performance assessment on his or her behalf.
  (3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), matters necessary for methods, procedures, standards, etc. of performance assessment shall be determined by the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency.
